  "adopted_reasons": {
    "through_hole": "Issue start value 5.5 kept: M5 normal clearance, same as the R6/R9 5.5 body holes.",
    "pocket_af": "Changed from the 8.5 start value to 8.4. 8.4 still clears the 8.0 envelope by 0.4 (0.2 per flat). With a nut whose corners are truncated like ISO 10511 (e_min/s = 8.79/8.0), a 7.68 across-flats nut reaches 4.22 mm corner radius: that locks against an 8.4 pocket (4.20 inscribed radius) but could spin in an 8.5 pocket (4.25). Sharp-corner nominal nuts lock in both. The N1 ladder coupon tests 8.3/8.4/8.5 physically.",
    "pocket_effective_depth": "Issue start value 5.5 kept: 0.5 over the 5.0 envelope height. The 0.2 overcut below the boss is not counted.",
    "nut_roof": "Issue start value 1.5 kept.",
    "nut_wall_min": "1.6 = issue minimum 1.5 plus 0.1 margin; it sets the boss depth perpendicular to the edge.",
    "plate_edge_to_axis": "Moved inward from the M3 3.9 so an assumed 10 mm head stays fully on the plate (0.5 margin) and the side boss stays outside the 40HP rail/panel X range.",
    "boss_half_length": "M3 14 mm boss length kept; 7.0 exceeds hex corner radius + 1.6 wall (6.45)."
  },
